 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the city of Buffalo to offer an optional twenty year\nretirement plan to firefighters Rhiannon Maguire and Jeffrey Brett",
    "basePrintNo": "S8686",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8686-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8686\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the city of Buffalo to offer an optional twenty year\nretirement plan to firefighters Rhiannon Maguire and Jeffrey Brett\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow the City of Buffalo to offer a\ntwenty-year retirement plan to two firefighters employed by the City\nwho, for reasons not ascribable to their own negligence, failed to make\na timely application to participate in such optional twenty-year retire-\nment plan.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the City of Buffalo to offer a retirement plan\npursuant to section 384-d of the retirement and social security law to\nRhiannon Maguire and Jeffrey Brett.\n\nSection 2 specifies that the City of Buffalo will bear responsibility\nfor all employer past service costs, which may be amortized over a ten-\nyear period.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRhiannon Maguire and Jeffrey Brett are firefighters employed by the City\nof Buffalo. Both firefighters were hired in Sept 2009, at a time when\nNew York State was transitioning to a new pension tier. Both had prior\npublic service, and both were given misinformation by a state represen-\ntative that they were not eligible to participate in the 20-year retire-\nment plan offered to other firefighters. This bill would authorize the\ncity of Buffalo to offer an optional twenty year retirement plan to\nfirefighters Rhiannon Maguire and Jeffrey Brett.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021: S.8771, died in Civil Service and Pensions.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nAs determined in Fiscal Note  2024-121, appended to this bill.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
